  "id": "EUVD-2026-64985",
  "enisaUuid": "9252cc72-9016-35ba-91ce-cd00331ede85",
  "description": "Multiple DrayTek VigorSwitch models contain a command injection vulnerability in the setDevice function. The vulnerability is caused by insufficient sanitization of the username, password, and location fields before command execution. A remote attacker can trigger this vulnerability via crafted input to execute arbitrary commands with root privileges. Exploitation requires valid administrative credentials for the device's web management interface.",
